#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter describes the use of &ksnapshot; for capturing screen images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksnapshot; may be started by one of several ways as described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may start &ksnapshot; by selecting it from the application launcher menu "
"<menuchoice> <guisubmenu>Applications</guisubmenu><guisubmenu>Graphics</"
"guisubmenu> <guimenuitem>Screen Capture Program &ksnapshot;</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may start &ksnapshot; by entering the following at the command prompt:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid "<prompt>%</prompt> <command>ksnapshot &amp;</command>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mini command line &krunner; (invoked with <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo>) may also be used to start &ksnapshot;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once &ksnapshot; starts, you will see a window like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:149 index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksnapshot; Preview Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Taking A Snapshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksnapshot; grabs an image of your entire desktop immediately after it is "
"started, but before it displays itself on screen. This allows you to quickly "
"create full-desktop screenshot images."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The snapshot taken by &ksnapshot; is displayed in the preview window, which "
"is located in the upper left of the &ksnapshot; application window. Below is "
"an example of the preview window from &ksnapshot;. Your preview will differ "
"depending on what you have displayed on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The snapshot can be saved by clicking on the <guibutton>Save As...</"
"guibutton> button. This opens the standard &kde; save dialog, where you can "
"choose the filename, the folder location, and the format that your snapshot "
"will be saved in. If multiple snapshots are taken, the filename is "
"automatically incremented to prevent you from overwriting previous "
"snapshots. You may however edit the filename to anything you wish, including "
"the name of a previously saved snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a snapshot of a single window, select the <guilabel>Window Under "
"Cursor</guilabel> combo box entry (next to the <guilabel>Capture mode</"
"guilabel> label), and then click on the <guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton> "
"button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your <guilabel>Snapshot delay</guilabel> settings you get "
"either a cross as the mouse pointer (for <guilabel>No delay</guilabel>), or "
"a standard mouse cursor which you can use to work with a program until the "
"delay is over and a snapshot is taken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With <guilabel>No delay</guilabel>, the snapshot is taken immediately when "
"you click into a window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ksnapshot; will display the new snapshot in the preview area, at which time "
"you can choose to save the new image (by pressing <guibutton>Save As...</"
"guibutton>) or to grab a new one, by pressing the <guibutton>New Snapshot</"
"guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a new snapshot of the entire desktop, select the <guilabel>Full "
"Screen</guilabel> combo box entry and then click on the <guibutton>New "
"Snapshot</guibutton> button. &ksnapshot; will now capture the entire desktop "
"if you press <guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similarly, to take a snapshot of a region, select the <guilabel>Region</"
"guilabel> combo box entry and set the <guilabel>Snapshot delay</guilabel> to "
"<guilabel>No delay</guilabel>, and then click on the <guibutton>New "
"Snapshot</guibutton> button. The mouse cursor will then change into a cross, "
"and you can then use the mouse to select the region you want to capture. To "
"take the snapshot press the &Enter; key or double click. Press &Esc; to quit."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To take a new snapshot of a section of a window, select the "
"<guilabel>Section of Window</guilabel> combo box entry and then click on the "
"<guibutton>New Snapshot</guibutton> button. With <guilabel>No delay</"
"guilabel> you get a cross as the mouse pointer and you have to click once "
"with the &LMB; into the window. The section of the window under the mouse "
"cursor is now highlighted with a red border. Move the mouse to the wanted "
"section and click the &LMB; to capture the screenshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have multiple screens, <guilabel>Current Screen</guilabel> captures "
"the screen containing the mouse cursor when the screenshot is taken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Additional Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Snapshot Delay"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Snapshot delay</guilabel> box allows you to enter an arbitrary "
"time delay, in seconds, between the time that you press the <guibutton>New "
"Snapshot</guibutton> button and the time that the snapshot is taken."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a delay time has been set, you do not have to click the mouse button to "
"capture a screenshot. This enables you to open a drop down menu, and take a "
"picture of it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exclude Window decorations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Include window decorations</guilabel> is enabled by default in "
"<guilabel>Window Under Cursor</guilabel> mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you only want to capture the application itself without the surrounding "
"window decoration, disable this option and take a new snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy to Clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you want to edit your snapshot in a graphics application without saving "
"the snapshot, just click <guibutton>Copy to Clipboard</guibutton> and insert "
"the image into a viewer or graphics application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Buttons"
msgstr "Botons"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two further buttons located at the bottom of the &ksnapshot; "
"window. Their function is described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "Ajuda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Gives you a menu where you can open the <guimenuitem>&ksnapshot; Handbook</"
"guimenuitem>, report a bug, switch the language for &ksnapshot; or get some "
"more information <guimenuitem>About &ksnapshot;</guimenuitem> and "
"<guimenuitem>About &kde;</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quit"
msgstr "Quitar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quits the &ksnapshot; application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "&DBus; Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ksnapshot; can be scripted using its &DBus; interface."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two ways to use the &DBus; interface: &Qt;'s &GUI; "
"<application>qdbusviewer</application> and the command line "
"<application>qdbus</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>&percnt;</prompt> <command>qdbus</command> will display all services "
"available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>&percnt;</prompt> <command>qdbus</command> <option>org.kde.ksnapshot-"
"`pidof -s ksnapshot`</option> will display the &DBus; interface for "
"&ksnapshot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>&percnt;</prompt> <command>qdbus</command> <option>org.kde.ksnapshot-"
"`pidof -s ksnapshot` /KSnapshot</option> will display methods for "
"controlling &ksnapshot;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information, please visit <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/"
"Development/Tutorials/D-Bus/Introduction\">&DBus; tutorial</ulink>."
msgstr ""

